  "notes": [
    "Replace the A/I factory in the sole dispatcher with the combined A/I/Case factory; do not start a second dispatcher.",
    "Select the investigation/lifecycle/Case-allocation policies explicitly. Query preparation is frozen with each Run; defaults are 3600 seconds before/after and 50 rows per log query, bounded by the Run policy.",
    "Case initial creates and claims an internal pending Run then binds the attempt in one PG transaction. E01 callers only receive accepted tasks.",
    "Retire external E11/E13 together with the HTTP adapter/Swagger. Mount asynchronous Case check/rerun; freeze comparison_context and previous actual Run once before C1-C6. Keep internal core primitives.",
    "Case scan_batch_size is explicit (example 100); lifecycle defaults stay 6 hours / 7 days. Service actors follow only the unique active event receiver, including capacity continuations. HTTP comparison links are adapter-owned.",
    "Legacy CLI case-prepare/case-start are removed from the candidate host/job entry points; case-create only accepts tasks.",
    "Steps8-10 are deferred; current knowledge behavior is not replaced by this fragment.",
    "Enabled dispatch requires all current A/I/Case handlers and IO contracts; absent or old contracts fail before consumption. Historical policies and artifacts remain readable but never select an old model path. Budgets remain configurable.",
    "This fragment does not authorize deployment, production restarts, consumer activation, Git push or old data cleanup."
  ],
  "required_execution_profiles": [
    "alert_io",
    "incident_io",
    "case_io"
  ]
